                <pb facs="0551" n="449" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg449"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5141: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-11-15T16:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 15,
                                1927—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10:15
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>68. Your telegram No. 32, November 14, 5 p.m. President Paz informed me this
                    morning that an investigation of reports from the region in question was ordered
                    by him yesterday. He said that reports received by him indicated that some
                    property had been destroyed and several Honduraneans had been killed at Santa
                    Rita and San <pb facs="0552" n="450" xml:id="pg450"/> Luis in Honduras by
                    American marines and constabulary forces and that Liberal civilians from
                    Nicaragua had accompanied the marines.</p>
                <p>President Paz stated that he believes that some Liberals, both Nica-raguans and
                    Honduraneans, by deceiving the marines are endeavoring to cause trouble between
                    Honduras and Nicaragua. Repeated to Nicaragua.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
